# sha256 of every tarball this port fetches at build time, one per line:
#     <sha256>  <filename>
#
# WHY: these tarballs are pulled with curl from a third-party mirror and cached in
# $PHOENIX_DISTFILES (default ~/.phoenix-distfiles/xorg) OUTSIDE the buildroot,
# keyed by basename and reused forever. Nothing verified them, unlike every
# framework-fetched anchor, which pins sha256= -- so this host built from a cache
# nothing checked while a clean room re-downloaded whatever the mirror served that
# day. _fetch_extract now verifies against this list before extracting and b_die's
# on a mismatch.
#
# The recorded values were cross-checked on 2026-09-04: two tarballs re-fetched
# from the recipe's own mirror agreed byte-for-byte with the cache, and several
# sums match widely published values. Mirror agreement is NOT a signature check.
#
# Adding a tarball: fetch it, `sha256sum` it, add the line. A file with no entry
# builds with a loud warning rather than failing, so a new fetch is visible but not
# blocked.
